## Exercise 1: Observing Exceptions (Program Crashes)

### Key Teaching Point: 
*"Look how the program crashes - this is why we need exception handling!"*

### Input Data:
```java
// Test cases that will be processed:
1. "CNT-2024-0001" with date "2024-01-15"  // Valid data
2. null contract ID                        // Will cause NullPointerException  
3. "INVALID_DATE" as date                  // Will cause ParseException
4. "CNT-ABCD-0001" contract ID            // Will cause NumberFormatException
5. "TOTALLY-WRONG-FORMAT" contract ID      // Will cause NumberFormatException
```

### Expected Console Output:
```
============================================================
EXERCISE 1: OBSERVING EXCEPTIONS IN CONTRACT PROCESSING
============================================================

=== Test Case 1: Valid Data ===
Testing valid contract ID and date...
    Validating contract ID: CNT-2024-0001
    Parsing date: 2024-01-15
✓ Contract ID validation result: true
✓ Date parsing result: Mon Jan 15 00:00:00 UTC 2024

=== Test Case 2: Null Contract ID ===
Testing null contract ID...
    Validating contract ID: null
✗ Exception caught: RuntimeException - java.lang.NullPointerException
Program crashed! Cannot continue with this approach.

=== Test Case 3: Invalid Date Format ===
Testing invalid date format...
    Parsing date: INVALID_DATE
✗ Exception caught: RuntimeException - java.text.ParseException: Unparseable date: "INVALID_DATE"
Program crashed! Cannot parse invalid date.

=== Test Case 4: Invalid Contract ID Format ===
Testing invalid contract ID format...
    Validating contract ID: CNT-ABCD-0001
✗ Exception caught: NumberFormatException - For input string: "ABCD"
Program crashed! Cannot parse non-numeric year.

=== Test Case 5: Malformed Contract ID ===
Testing malformed contract ID...
    Validating contract ID: TOTALLY-WRONG-FORMAT
✗ Exception caught: NumberFormatException - For input string: "TOTALLY"
Program crashed! Cannot parse malformed ID.

============================================================
CONCLUSION: Without exception handling, the program
crashes on invalid data and cannot process remaining items!
============================================================
```

### Teaching Moment:
*Point out how each exception stops the program completely - very dramatic for students!*

